      "problem": "| $5$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $?$ | $30$ |\n| $25$ | $50$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing from the ratio table?",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $5:10$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{10}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($5$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($10$).\n\nWe can make a denominator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5\\times 3}{10\\times 3} & =\\frac{15}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| $5$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $15$ | $30$ |\n| $25$ | $50$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $15.$",
